{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbpXb6e4DhiyEnzM69x8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The adsorption energy of atomic oxygen on Cu(111) is **−4.84 ± 0.4 eV**, at the fcc hollow site. It is referenced to an isolated O atom. I posted it to the board as `cfa0f4f8`, which closes the team's request.\n\n**Premise:** this is a 0 K relaxation energy, so simulation length doesn't matter. The referee agreed (premise_check: pass). The one real concern was whether the model gives a sensible energy for a lone O atom. I tested that directly (see Validation).\n\n**Method:** I used the MACE-MPA-0 model (float64, GPU) on a 4-layer Cu(111) slab, 3×3 cell (1/9 monolayer), with the bottom two layers fixed. Oxygen was relaxed from four starting sites:\n\n| Site | E_ads (eV), 1/9 ML | E_ads (eV), 1/4 ML |\n|---|---|---|\n| **fcc** | **−4.84** | −4.90 |\n| hcp | −4.78 | −4.84 |\n| ontop | −3.08 | −3.13 |\n| bridge | relaxes into fcc | relaxes into fcc |\n\nGoing from 4 to 6 layers changes the answer by less than 0.003 eV. Referenced to half an O₂ molecule instead, the fcc value is −1.70 eV.\n\n**Validation:** each check reuses the same model and setup.\n- **Cu lattice constant:** 3.640 Å, against 3.615 Å measured.\n- **Cu cohesive energy:** 3.50 eV, against about 3.49 eV measured.\n- **O₂ bond length:** 1.235 Å.\n- **O₂ binding energy:** 6.29 eV relative to the model's own lone O atom, close to the PBE functional's value (about 6.2 eV). This is the key check: it shows the model's isolated-O energy behaves like the gas-phase O atom from that standard DFT method. So −4.84 eV should be read as that method's answer, not as an experimental value.\n\n**Uncertainty (±0.4 eV)** covers:\n- **Choice of DFT method (the largest term):** PBE overbinds the O atom relative to O₂ by about 0.5 eV per molecule. If I combine my O₂-referenced result with the measured O₂ binding energy (about 5.21 eV), I get about −4.30 eV instead.\n- **Spread in published DFT values:** about −4.3 eV (Xu & Mavrikakis, Surf. Sci. 494, 131 (2001)) to −5.0 eV (fcc site, a more recent study). I found the first only in the abstract and could not confirm from it whether that site is fcc or hcp.\n- **Coverage:** about 0.07 eV between 1/9 and 1/4 monolayer.\n- **Model error versus DFT:** about 0.1 eV, an estimate I did not measure.\n\nThere is no adsorption reference in `/data/calibration/tier1.json`. No zero-point or thermal corrections are included. I added no flags, because the model is within its training domain and the checks above passed. The caveats are written into the result's note.\n\nSources:\n- [Xu & Mavrikakis, Surf. Sci. 2001 (abstract)](https://data.zhenzhi.com/details/1/867115130)\n- [Cu(211) step study citing −4.3 eV for Cu(111)](https://data.zhenzhi.com/details/1/888079892)\n- [Recent DFT study (fcc −5.000 / hcp −4.905 eV)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.13036)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":694,"cache_read_input_tokens":36161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":694,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68e3c0ea-1e39-4c13-9e54-6a3ef38db9e4","uuid":"84e70102-88b1-46ea-84bb-bc0386f8e934","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:33:32.270Z","request_id":"req_011CgbpXakJaKYrhGGNBsEwj"}
